        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"stael-corinne-e565b0348bdf4b38\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Corinne’s embedded “je vous aime” straightforwardly avows her present love for Oswald and supplies the reason for her devotion and visit. It does not itself undertake a commitment: indeed, her speech resists Oswald’s attempt to construe her conduct as creating a marital obligation. Although the surrounding passage describes an irresistible impulse and intense concern, the words occur in a composed explanatory argument rather than as an affect-driven verbal discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The adjoining claim that she is devoted to Oswald creates slight performative pressure, but the love clause itself presents an existing feeling as the ground of that devotion rather than enacting an undertaking.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Corinne says the words directly to Oswald, syntactically embedded in the causal/temporal clause “quand je vous aime” within a longer spoken explanation.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Corinne is reassuring Oswald that visiting him has not socially compromised her. She openly acknowledges loving him while distinguishing that love and her devoted care from the reputational breach that, in Oswald’s view, would obligate him to marry her. The narrator calls her words natural and sincere, supporting a genuine avowal, while Oswald’s frustration that Italian custom imposes “aucun lien” reinforces the absence of commitment-creating force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“je ne sais s'ils me blâment de vous aimer, mais sûrement ils ne me blâmeront pas d'être dévouée à vous, quand je vous aime.”\",\"supports\":\"The highlighted clause presents Corinne’s love as an existing fact that explains her devotion, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Corinne rejects Oswald’s assumption that her visit has compromised her and explains that women in Rome may properly aid a suffering friend.\",\"supports\":\"Her speech denies that her conduct has generated the obligation Oswald imagines, weighing strongly against P for the love clause.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narrator describes what Oswald hears as “ces paroles si naturelles et si sincères.”\",\"supports\":\"Narratorial framing supports the love avowal’s presented sincerity, while not changing its fundamentally truth-conditional mode.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Oswald resents that Roman social freedom leaves him happiness “sans lui imposer aucun lien” and wishes honor would command him to marry.\",\"supports\":\"The passage explicitly locates the desired obligation outside Corinne’s utterance, further disfavoring P.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified as affirmative present-tense “je vous aime” in a main-or-embedded syntactic family and retained as a valid explicit I-love-you instance.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the classified expression is an affirmative, present love predication despite its embedded syntax.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. The surrounding devotion, urgency, social argument, and sincerity are contextual features and do not require P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
